{"id": "EUVD-2026-101060", "enisaUuid": "271b2ae9-cb61-3615-9bf5-7fdb428f1a68", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: sequencing: fix NULL-pointer dereference in pwrseq_device_register()\n\nIf dev_set_name() fails in pwrseq_device_register(), we jump to the\nerr_put_pwrseq label before initializing pwrseq->targets.\npwrseq_release() will try to iterate over targets unconditionally and\nsubsequently dereference an invalid pointer. Move the call to\ndev_set_name() after the list head is initialized.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2fb51ec8920279e9e908010f37b448775f42eff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2890c1eb96d1dd0bec1cce5fbc4ed5af1dfd55d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/efe21a5c5bfe23bd30a8e4ba4e2b04ae265348bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/242da4318d97380741516b595af3920207b2f0f1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98411", "GHSA-32c9-x322-76xq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22f5d529-f6d2-3a7c-ae19-22d0f2c5bfdf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "6a06f24c-c34e-305c-b5d1-33a7634d2a6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "249ebf3f65f8530beb2cbfb91bff1d83ba88d23c <a2890c1eb96d1dd0bec1cce5fbc4ed5af1dfd55d"}, {"id": "876b750c-a628-3385-9361-332cfb028549", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "893ea456-e8f0-31aa-bbae-e572a88d6fd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "249ebf3f65f8530beb2cbfb91bff1d83ba88d23c <242da4318d97380741516b595af3920207b2f0f1"}, {"id": "9cbfba94-668d-3dbb-84cb-f22feb7382d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b6a07f53-e647-34cc-ad29-ad54eb1dc84f", "product": {"name": "